{"assets":["/statement-assets/02d29e5c38fd8eafe80a4833c439d4ff78888209fdc01073fd3dacb9ba42c596.png","/statement-assets/e8c5ace148dc73721b35a436abc49859ba7bc8dbdba87f2ff0c8070c1186ceb5.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"10","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Cinema Cashier"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All cinema halls in Berland are rectangles with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":" seats each, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an odd number. Rows and seats are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":". For safety reasons people, who come to the box office to buy tickets, are not allowed to choose seats themselves. Formerly the choice was made by a cashier, but now this is the responsibility of a special seating program. It was found out that the large majority of Berland's inhabitants go to the cinema in order to watch a movie, that's why they want to sit as close to the hall center as possible. Moreover, a company of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"M"},{"kind":"text","text":" people, who come to watch a movie, want necessarily to occupy "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"M"},{"kind":"text","text":" successive seats in one row. Let's formulate the algorithm, according to which the program chooses seats and sells tickets. As the request for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"M"},{"kind":"text","text":" seats comes, the program should determine the row number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[yl, yr]"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the seats numbers in this row, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yr - yl + 1 = M"},{"kind":"text","text":". From all such possible variants as a final result the program should choose the one with the minimum function value of total seats remoteness from the center. Say, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/02d29e5c38fd8eafe80a4833c439d4ff78888209fdc01073fd3dacb9ba42c596.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the row and the seat numbers of the most \"central\" seat. Then the function value of seats remoteness from the hall center is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e8c5ace148dc73721b35a436abc49859ba7bc8dbdba87f2ff0c8070c1186ceb5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the amount of minimum function values is more than one, the program should choose the one that is closer to the screen (i.e. the row number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" is lower). If the variants are still multiple, it should choose the one with the minimum "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yl"},{"kind":"text","text":". If you did not get yet, your task is to simulate the work of this program. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ N ≤ 1000, 1 ≤ K ≤ 99"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the amount of requests and the hall size respectively. The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Mi"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the range "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[1, K]"},{"kind":"text","text":" — requests to the program."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines. In the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line output «-1» (without quotes), if it is impossible to find "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Mi"},{"kind":"text","text":" successive seats in one row, otherwise output three numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x, yl, yr"},{"kind":"text","text":". Separate the numbers with a space."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1 1\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 3\n1 2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2 2\n1 1 2\n3 1 3\n2 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"10B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/10/problem/B"}